<title>JAPAN: Japan two-year note auction lowest price of 100.10.</title>
<headline>Japan two-year note auction lowest price of 100.10.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance said that its auction on Thursday of 120 billion yen of two-year government notes produced the following results:</p>
<p>Lowest price	 100.10    Stop rate	   0.649 pct</p>
<p>Average price	100.12    Average yield     0.636 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   329.7 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	116.5 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 59.6100 pct Issue date    Dec 20, 1996   Maturity    Dec 21, 1998</p>
</text>
